From 18f5e98f200e311454eafcc3ee903d054b420f1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 16:12:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add in-app legal pages and policy consent

- New public pages at /legal: Terms of Service, Privacy Policy, Cookie
  Policy, Plans/Billing & Cancellation, Refund Policy, Copyright & Content,
  Accessibility. Served by the app so sign-up, checkout and viewer links
  resolve while the marketing site is private. All 19 existing policy links
  (footer, sign-up, checkout, viewer, upload notice) now point to them.
- Billing, refund and retention text follows docs/approved-launch-policies.md
  (Basic USD399/month or USD4,548.60/year, automatic renewal, cancellation at
  period end, refund rules, 90-day retrieval). Privacy and cookie text
  describes current behaviour: one essential session cookie, no analytics or
  ad trackers, IPs in audit logs, hashed IPs for rate limits, and the
  processors used (Render, Cloudflare R2, Stripe, email provider, maps).
- Pages show a 'Draft for owner and legal review' notice until
  LEGAL_TERMS_APPROVED=1. Operator name, contact, postal address and
  governing law come from LEGAL_ENTITY_NAME, LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL,
  LEGAL_POSTAL_ADDRESS and LEGAL_GOVERNING_LAW; nothing is hard-coded.
- Employee and Enterprise invite setup now require accepting the Terms and
  Privacy Policy and record the accepted versions, as sign-up already does.
  Account terms and privacy versions bumped to 2026-11-03.
- Notices on the client code page and the Enterprise request form.
- Tests: tests/test_legal_pages.py (6). Per-module results match main.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HbptFaAKPeT417LTNgj5bU
